Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 06:54:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 036/154] build: list the portable atrium sources outside the
 is_mac arm
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thirty-one entries move out: every renamed .cc and the headers with no .mm
sibling. Eleven .mm files and their headers stay inside, which is the whole of
what is genuinely AppKit today.

Measured on the real Linux GN output rather than argued: gn gen for
target_os=linux succeeds, and //chrome/browser/ui:ui carries 35 atrium sources
with zero .mm. Control: the same query before this change returns 4.

chrome_context already had no .mm sources - the rename in 443.1 did that.

These files do not COMPILE on Linux yet. That is H3.7 and H3.8. What this
unblocks is generation, which is the step everything else waits behind.

macOS builds unchanged: zero errors, zero warnings, same targets.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 55 +++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 5528310e0cb87..eef299e55832f 100644
